    "### Tools beyond the course material\n",
    "\n",
    "Almost everything here uses methods from the class notebooks. These are the exceptions:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Tool | Where | Why we used it |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `scipy.stats.chi2_contingency` and Cramér's V (`np.sqrt`) | `chi_square_test` helper | tests whether the Top 10 rate is different between groups, and how strong the link is |\n",
    "| `scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu` | `mann_whitney_test` helper | tests whether a number (like word count) is different for Top 10 songs, without assuming a bell curve |\n",
    "| `ax.bar_label` | bar charts | writes each bar's value on the chart, so you don't have to guess it |\n"
    "| `.quantile(0.02)` | Step 9 | finds the slowest 2% of lyrics in each genre, to flag lyrics that may be cut short |\n",
    "| `ch.isspace()` | Step 10 | treats every kind of space (spaces, tabs, line breaks) as a space when we keep only letters, numbers and spaces |\n",
    "| `.drop_duplicates` | Steps 4 and 5 | keeps one row per song and artist after we stack the split credits |\n",
    "| `invert_yaxis` | Chart 13 | puts chart position 1 at the top, like the real chart |\n",
    "| `showfliers=False`, `sharey=True` | Charts 5 and 6 | hides extreme outliers in the box plots; gives the two month panels the same scale |\n",
    "| `.duplicated` | Steps 1 and 3 | counts rows (or keys) that appear more than once |\n",
    "| `.str.contains` | Step 4 | checks whether a credit contains a word like \"featuring\" (plain text, no regex) |\n",
    "| `.str.len` | Steps 9 and 10 | counts the characters in the lyrics, or the words and lines after a split |\n",
    "| `.sample` | Step 5 | picks 200 random songs to recount by hand |\n",
    "| `.count` | Steps 2 and 10 | counts the weeks a song was on the chart, and how many times a line appears in a song |\n",
    "| `.values` | `chi_square_test`, Step 8 | gets the plain numbers out of a table or a dictionary |\n",
    "| `os.path.exists` | Step 1 | checks whether a file is already on disk before reading or uploading it |\n",
    "| `plt.gca` | Chart 13 | gets the current chart, so we can flip its y-axis |\n",
    "| `rot=` | Chart 9 | keeps the bar labels horizontal |\n",
    "| `value_counts(dropna=False)` | Step 8 | counts the songs in each genre, including the ones with no genre |"
