  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75ecce4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5. Each artist's chart history before the song debuted\n",
    "\n",
    "First we find the week each song **first** reached the Top 10. We need it below: an earlier song\n",
    "only counts as a hit if it was *already* a hit when the new song came out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "c91f6345",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.753809Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.753742Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.801620Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.801157Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "songs with a first Top 10 week: 5303\n",
      "songs with top10 = True: 5303\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# The first week each song reached the Top 10. Songs that never did get a blank.\n",
    "top10_weeks = weekly[weekly['position'] <= 10]\n",
    "first_top10 = top10_weeks.groupby(['title', 'artist']).agg(first_top10_date=('chart_date', 'min')).reset_index()\n",
    "songs = pd.merge(songs, first_top10, on=['title', 'artist'], how='left', validate='one_to_one')\n",
    "\n",
    "# These two numbers must match.\n",
    "print('songs with a first Top 10 week:', songs['first_top10_date'].notna().sum())\n",
    "print('songs with top10 = True:', songs['top10'].sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "54b35c89",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Then we stack the split columns into one row per (song, artist). A song credited to \"Bruno Mars &\n",
    "Cardi B\" shows up once under each artist."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "8bca3eb3",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.802662Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.802597Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.846200Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.845787Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "songs: 32688 -> song-artist rows: 39939\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Make one row per (song, artist), so every artist in a credit gets the song.\n",
    "pieces = []\n",
    "for column in artist_columns.columns:\n",
    "    piece = songs[['title', 'artist', 'debut_date', 'top10', 'first_top10_date']].copy()\n",
    "    piece['artist_name'] = artist_columns[column].str.strip()\n",
    "    pieces.append(piece)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Stack the pieces. Credits with fewer artists leave blanks, so we drop those.\n",
    "artist_songs = pd.concat(pieces)\n",
    "artist_songs = artist_songs.dropna(subset=['artist_name'])\n",
    "artist_songs = artist_songs[artist_songs['artist_name'] != '']\n",
    "artist_songs = artist_songs.drop_duplicates(subset=['title', 'artist', 'artist_name'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print('songs:', len(songs), '-> song-artist rows:', len(artist_songs))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "28e7d4fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Next we pair every 2018+ song with all songs by its lead artist and keep only the songs that\n",
    "debuted **strictly earlier**. Songs released in the same week don't count as \"earlier\", so nothing\n",
    "from the song's own debut leaks in.\n",
    "\n",
    "An earlier song counts as a **hit** only if its first Top 10 week came before the new song's debut\n",
    "week. Our first version counted every earlier song that *eventually* reached the Top 10, even if it\n",
    "got there after the new song came out. Azaan found this leak when he reviewed our notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "7a673d31",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.847268Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.847201Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.888120Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.887608Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rename the columns, so we can pair each song with the lead artist's other songs.\n",
    "earlier_songs = artist_songs.rename(columns={\n",
    "    'title': 'earlier_title', 'artist': 'earlier_artist', 'debut_date': 'earlier_debut',\n",
    "    'top10': 'earlier_top10', 'first_top10_date': 'earlier_first_top10', 'artist_name': 'primary_artist'})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pair every 2018+ song with every song by the same lead artist.\n",
    "recent = songs[songs['debut_date'] >= '2018-01-01']\n",
    "pairs = pd.merge(recent[['title', 'artist', 'debut_date', 'primary_artist']],\n",
    "                 earlier_songs, on='primary_artist', how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only songs that debuted before this one, so we don't use future information.\n",
    "earlier = pairs[pairs['earlier_debut'] < pairs['debut_date']].copy()\n",
    "# An earlier song counts as a hit only if it was ALREADY a Top 10 hit when this song debuted.\n",
    "earlier['hit_before_debut'] = earlier['earlier_first_top10'] < earlier['debut_date']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "51274859",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.889368Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.889297Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.929727Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.929334Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "recent songs: 5342\n",
      "(song, earlier song) pairs: 241042\n",
      "songs with any history: 4831\n",
      "songs whose hit count drops with the fix: 444\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Count each song's earlier entries and earlier hits. True counts as 1, so the sum is a count.\n",
    "# eventual_top10s is the old count, which also counted later hits. We keep it only to compare.\n",
    "history = earlier.groupby(['title', 'artist']).agg(\n",
    "    prior_entries=('earlier_title', 'count'),\n",
    "    prior_top10s=('hit_before_debut', 'sum'),\n",
    "    eventual_top10s=('earlier_top10', 'sum'),\n",
    ").reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('recent songs:', len(recent))\n",
    "print('(song, earlier song) pairs:', len(earlier))\n",
    "print('songs with any history:', len(history))\n",
    "print('songs whose hit count drops with the fix:', (history['eventual_top10s'] > history['prior_top10s']).sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9f9cb45c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Two checks for leaks. A song must never count itself, and a slow recount of 200 random songs, one at\n",
    "a time with the same \"hit before debut\" rule, must give the same numbers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "ccc2aea9",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.930817Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:35.930724Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.299929Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.299514Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "songs counted in their own history: 0\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "mismatches in 200 recounted songs: 0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Check 1: no song is ever counted in its own history.\n",
    "self_counted = (earlier['earlier_title'] == earlier['title']) & (earlier['earlier_artist'] == earlier['artist'])\n",
    "print('songs counted in their own history:', self_counted.sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check 2: recount 200 random songs the slow way, one at a time, and compare.\n",
    "sample = recent.sample(200, random_state=42)\n",
    "mismatches = 0\n",
    "for i in sample.index:\n",
    "    same_artist = artist_songs[artist_songs['artist_name'] == sample.loc[i, 'primary_artist']]\n",
    "    before = same_artist[same_artist['debut_date'] < sample.loc[i, 'debut_date']]\n",
    "    # Earlier songs that were already hits in this song's debut week.\n",
    "    known_hits = before[before['first_top10_date'] < sample.loc[i, 'debut_date']]\n",
    "    found = history[(history['title'] == sample.loc[i, 'title']) & (history['artist'] == sample.loc[i, 'artist'])]\n",
    "    if len(known_hits) != found['prior_top10s'].sum():\n",
    "        mismatches = mismatches + 1\n",
    "print('mismatches in 200 recounted songs:', mismatches)"
   ]
  },
