   "source": [
    "### Step 8. Broad genre\n",
    "\n",
    "MusicBrainz uses hundreds of detailed labels (\"cloud rap\", \"dance-pop\"). We map each label to one\n",
    "of eight broad genres with simple keyword rules, add up the votes for each broad genre, and pick\n",
    "the one with the most votes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Latin** means Spanish- or Portuguese-language Latin American music, so Brazilian funk is Latin,\n",
    "while reggae and dancehall are \"other\". Keywords match whole words, so \"rap\" matches \"pop rap\" but\n",
    "not the inside of another word."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "7ee3f14b",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.357497Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.357429Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.359994Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.359638Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Keywords for each broad genre. A one-word keyword must match a whole word of the label\n",
    "# (\"rap\" matches \"pop rap\" but not \"grape\"). A two-word keyword must appear as a phrase.\n",
    "latin_words = ['latin', 'latino', 'latina', 'reggaeton', 'regueton', 'salsa', 'bachata', 'cumbia',\n",
    "               'corrido', 'corridos', 'banda', 'mariachi', 'tejano', 'merengue', 'dembow', 'norteño',\n",
    "               'norteno', 'ranchera', 'mexican', 'mexicano', 'bolero', 'flamenco', 'samba', 'bossa',\n",
    "               'brazilian', 'brasileiro', 'brasileira', 'carioca', 'ostentação', 'brega', 'sertanejo',\n",
    "               'español', 'espanol', 'portuguese']\n",
    "country_words = ['country', 'bluegrass', 'americana', 'honky', 'nashville', 'urban cowboy']\n",
    "hiphop_words = ['hip hop', 'hiphop', 'rap', 'trap', 'drill', 'grime', 'crunk', 'boom bap', 'bounce',\n",
    "                'hyphy', 'dirty south', 'rage', 'plugg', 'horrorcore', 'ratchet']\n",
    "rnb_words = ['funk', 'funky', 'funktronica', 'motown', 'new jack swing', 'quiet storm', 'doo wop']\n",
    "rock_words = ['rock', 'punk', 'metal', 'grunge', 'indie', 'alternative', 'emo', 'shoegaze',\n",
    "              'blackgaze', 'britpop', 'new wave', 'psychedelia']\n",
    "dance_words = ['electronic', 'electronica', 'electro', 'edm', 'house', 'techno', 'trance', 'dubstep',\n",
    "               'dance', 'disco', 'club', 'rave', 'drum and bass', 'dnb', 'bass', 'synthwave',\n",
    "               'eurodance', 'hardstyle', 'garage', 'trip hop', 'complextro', 'downtempo', 'leftfield',\n",
    "               'indietronica', 'jungle', 'ambient', 'tronica', 'breakbeat', 'moombahton', 'brostep',\n",
    "               'ebm', 'hardcore']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "b8400a8d",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.360914Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.360853Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.362643Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.362276Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Does a genre label contain one of the keywords?\n",
    "def has_keyword(label, keywords):\n",
    "    # Treat \"hip-hop\" the same as \"hip hop\".\n",
    "    label = label.replace('-', ' ')\n",
    "    words = label.split()\n",
    "    for keyword in keywords:\n",
    "        # A two-word keyword: look for the phrase.\n",
    "        if ' ' in keyword and keyword in label:\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "        # A one-word keyword: it must be a whole word.\n",
    "        if keyword in words:\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "    return False"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "45675c38",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The rules are checked in order and the first match wins. So \"latin pop\" is Latin and \"country pop\"\n",
    "is country, while \"pop rap\" is rap and \"dance-pop\" is pop."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "c76f551c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.363522Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.363464Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.365503Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.365204Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Turn one MusicBrainz label into a broad genre. The rules are checked in order and the first match wins.\n",
    "def broad_genre(label):\n",
    "    label = label.lower().strip()\n",
    "    if 'dancehall' in label:\n",
    "        # Dancehall is Jamaican music, not dance music.\n",
    "        return 'other'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, latin_words):\n",
    "        return 'Latin'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, country_words):\n",
    "        return 'country'\n",
    "    elif label.endswith('pop'):\n",
    "        # dance-pop, synth-pop, k-pop and so on.\n",
    "        return 'pop'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, ['soul', 'r&b', 'rnb']):\n",
    "        # This comes before rap, so \"trap soul\" counts as R&B.\n",
    "        return 'R&B'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, hiphop_words):\n",
    "        return 'hip-hop/rap'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, rnb_words):\n",
    "        return 'R&B'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, rock_words):\n",
    "        return 'rock/alternative'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, dance_words):\n",
    "        return 'dance/electronic'\n",
    "    elif has_keyword(label, ['pop']):\n",
    "        return 'pop'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'other'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "7f67afb2",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.366576Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.366515Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.368432Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.368148Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Add up the MusicBrainz votes for each broad genre, e.g. {'hip-hop/rap': 4, 'pop': 1}.\n",
    "def genre_votes(names, counts):\n",
    "    votes = {}\n",
    "    if pd.isna(names):\n",
    "        return votes\n",
    "    # Labels are stored like 'pop|dance-pop', and vote counts the same way.\n",
    "    name_list = names.split('|')\n",
    "    # With no stored counts, each label gets one vote.\n",
    "    count_list = [1] * len(name_list)\n",
    "    if not pd.isna(counts):\n",
    "        count_list = [int(c) for c in str(counts).split('|')]\n",
    "    for name, count in zip(name_list, count_list):\n",
    "        genre = broad_genre(name)\n",
    "        votes[genre] = votes.get(genre, 0) + count\n",
    "    return votes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d225d1bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "If a song has no genre, we use the lead artist's. If two genres tie, the artist's votes break the\n",
    "tie. If they still tie, the song is called \"mixed\"."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "86f64765",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.369571Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.369499Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.371880Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.371487Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pick one genre per song: the genre with the most votes wins.\n",
    "def song_genre(row):\n",
    "    song_votes = genre_votes(row['song_genres'], row['song_genre_counts'])\n",
    "    artist_votes = genre_votes(row['artist_genres'], row['artist_genre_counts'])\n",
    "    # No song genres: use the artist's genres instead.\n",
    "    if len(song_votes) == 0:\n",
    "        song_votes = artist_votes\n",
    "        artist_votes = {}\n",
    "    # No genres at all: leave it blank.\n",
    "    if len(song_votes) == 0:\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    top = max(song_votes.values())\n",
    "    leaders = [genre for genre in song_votes if song_votes[genre] == top]\n",
    "    if len(leaders) == 1:\n",
    "        return leaders[0]\n",
    "    # A tie: the artist's votes decide. If those tie too, the song is 'mixed'.\n",
    "    best = max([artist_votes.get(genre, 0) for genre in leaders])\n",
    "    winners = [genre for genre in leaders if artist_votes.get(genre, 0) == best]\n",
    "    if best > 0 and len(winners) == 1:\n",
    "        return winners[0]\n",
    "    return 'mixed'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "f46d7cb5",
