   "source": [
    "# Give every song its genre. axis=1 runs the function on each row.\n",
    "songs['primary_genre'] = songs.apply(song_genre, axis=1)\n",
    "# dropna=False also counts the songs with no genre.\n",
    "songs['primary_genre'].value_counts(dropna=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c584b0ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 9. Fix bad song lengths, and flag lyrics that look cut short\n",
    "\n",
    "The length from LRCLIB is sometimes a whole album's length or a 0-2 second placeholder. We trust a\n",
    "length between 30 seconds and 10 minutes. Otherwise we use the MusicBrainz length."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "bc325d8a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.493632Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.493565Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.496917Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.496603Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "songs with an unusable LRCLIB duration: 382\n",
      "repaired with the MusicBrainz length: 306\n",
      "still unusable: 76\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Song length from LRCLIB. Under 30 seconds or over 10 minutes can't be right.\n",
    "songs['duration_used'] = songs['duration']\n",
    "bad = (songs['duration'] < 30) | (songs['duration'] > 600) | songs['duration'].isna()\n",
    "print('songs with an unusable LRCLIB duration:', bad.sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use the MusicBrainz length instead (it is in milliseconds, so divide by 1000).\n",
    "songs.loc[bad, 'duration_used'] = songs.loc[bad, 'recording_length_ms'] / 1000\n",
    "# If neither source is believable, leave it blank.\n",
    "still_bad = (songs['duration_used'] < 30) | (songs['duration_used'] > 600)\n",
    "songs.loc[still_bad, 'duration_used'] = np.nan\n",
    "print('repaired with the MusicBrainz length:', bad.sum() - songs['duration_used'].isna().sum())\n",
    "print('still unusable:', songs['duration_used'].isna().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ffde1f35",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Some lyric uploads are cut short. Characters per second shows them, but rap has many more words per\n",
    "second than country. So a song is flagged when it is in the slowest 2% *of its own genre*. Only the\n",
    "check in Phase 1, Q4 uses this flag."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "c4f5ef72",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.497981Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.497913Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.503934Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.503536Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "lyrics flagged as possibly cut short: 110\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Lyrics that look cut short have too few characters for the song's length.\n",
    "songs['lyrics_chars'] = songs['plain_lyrics'].str.len()\n",
    "songs['chars_per_sec'] = songs['lyrics_chars'] / songs['duration_used']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Rap is much denser than country, so we flag the slowest 2% within each genre.\n",
    "cutoffs = songs.groupby('primary_genre')['chars_per_sec'].quantile(0.02)\n",
    "songs['genre_cutoff'] = songs['primary_genre'].map(cutoffs)\n",
    "# Songs with no genre use the cut-off for all songs.\n",
    "songs['genre_cutoff'] = songs['genre_cutoff'].fillna(songs['chars_per_sec'].quantile(0.02))\n",
    "songs['lyrics_suspect_short'] = songs['chars_per_sec'] < songs['genre_cutoff']\n",
    "print('lyrics flagged as possibly cut short:', songs['lyrics_suspect_short'].sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d68ed889",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 10. Lyric features\n",
    "\n",
    "First we remove section tags like `[Chorus]` and `[Verse 2: Drake]`. We cut out everything from a\n",
    "`[` to the next `]`, which also removes timestamps like `[00:12.34]`. Then we keep only letters,\n",
    "numbers and apostrophes. Both steps are plain loops, no regex.\n",
    "\n",
    "Songs with no lyrics, and instrumentals, stay **blank**, never 0: a song without lyrics didn't have\n",
    "zero words, we just don't know."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "c4064beb",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.504835Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.504774Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.511248Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.510924Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "songs with lyrics text: 5310\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Remove section tags like [Chorus] or [Verse 2: Drake], and timestamps like [00:12.34]:\n",
    "# cut out everything from a '[' to the next ']'.\n",
    "clean = []\n",
    "for text in songs['plain_lyrics']:\n",
    "    if pd.notna(text):\n",
    "        while '[' in text and ']' in text[text.index('['):]:\n",
    "            start = text.index('[')\n",
    "            end = text.index(']', start)\n",
    "            text = text[:start] + text[end + 1:]\n",
    "    clean.append(text)\n",
    "songs['lyrics_clean'] = clean\n",
    "\n",
    "# Instrumentals have no lyrics.\n",
    "songs.loc[songs['instrumental'] == True, 'lyrics_clean'] = np.nan\n",
    "print('songs with lyrics text:', songs['lyrics_clean'].notna().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "91a2630f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.512170Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:36.512115Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.443313Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.442828Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Lowercase the lyrics and keep only letters, numbers, apostrophes and spaces.\n",
    "# Every other character (punctuation, accents) becomes a space. Line breaks stay.\n",
    "keep_chars = \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789'\"\n",
    "lyrics_words = []\n",
    "for text in songs['lyrics_clean'].str.lower():\n",
    "    if pd.isna(text):\n",
    "        lyrics_words.append(text)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        letters = []\n",
    "        for ch in text:\n",
    "            if ch in keep_chars or ch.isspace():\n",
    "                letters.append(ch)\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                letters.append(' ')\n",
    "        lyrics_words.append(''.join(letters))\n",
    "songs['lyrics_words'] = lyrics_words"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "960c38dd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Unique word ratio** measures vocabulary: \"baby baby baby oh\" has 4 words but only 2 different\n",
    "ones, so its ratio is 2 ÷ 4 = 0.5."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 40,
   "id": "8b8d3c5a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.444674Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.444608Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.684688Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.684040Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Two lyric measures. Songs with no words get a blank, never 0.\n",
    "songs['word_count'] = songs['lyrics_words'].str.split().str.len()\n",
    "songs.loc[songs['word_count'] == 0, 'word_count'] = np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "# Unique word ratio: different words / all words. set() keeps each word once.\n",
    "def unique_word_ratio(text):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(text) or len(text.split()) == 0:\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    words = text.split()\n",
    "    return len(set(words)) / len(words)\n",
    "\n",
    "songs['unique_word_ratio'] = songs['lyrics_words'].apply(unique_word_ratio)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "04df9da5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Average line length** is words per line. **Repetition score** is the share of lines that appear\n",
    "more than once in the song."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "35353fe5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.686006Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.685930Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.800904Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.800519Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split lyrics into non-empty lines, with extra spaces tidied so equal lines match.\n",
    "def lyric_lines(text):\n",
    "    lines = []\n",
    "    for line in text.split('\\n'):\n",
    "        line = ' '.join(line.split())\n",
    "        if line != '':\n",
    "            lines.append(line)\n",
    "    return lines\n",
    "\n",
    "# Average words per line.\n",
    "line_counts = songs['lyrics_words'].dropna().apply(lyric_lines).str.len()\n",
    "songs['avg_line_length'] = songs['word_count'] / line_counts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 42,
   "id": "bf03773f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.802083Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:37.802023Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.132459Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.132003Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Repetition score: the share of lines that appear more than once in the song.\n",
    "def repetition_score(text):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(text) or len(lyric_lines(text)) == 0:\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    lines = lyric_lines(text)\n",
    "    repeated = 0\n",
    "    for line in lines:\n",
    "        if lines.count(line) > 1:\n",
    "            repeated = repeated + 1\n",
    "    return repeated / len(lines)\n",
    "\n",
    "songs['repetition_score'] = songs['lyrics_words'].apply(repetition_score)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "7eafe1cc",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.133492Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.133431Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.480036Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-19T00:26:38.479564Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Strong profanity only. Mild words like \"damn\" and \"hell\" are left out on purpose.\n",
    "# Words that start with these also count, e.g. \"fucking\" or \"bitches\".\n",
    "profane_starts = ['fuck', 'shit', 'bitch', 'nigga', 'nigger', 'cunt', 'pussy', 'motherfuck',\n",
    "                  'mothafuck', 'asshole', 'bastard', 'whore', 'slut']\n",
    "# These only count as whole words, so \"hoe\" doesn't match \"shoe\".\n",
    "profane_words = ['dick', 'dicks', 'cock', 'hoe', 'hoes']\n",
    "\n",
    "def has_profanity(text):\n",
    "    if pd.isna(text) or len(text.split()) == 0:\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    for word in text.split():\n",
    "        if word in profane_words:\n",
    "            return True\n",
    "        for start in profane_starts:\n",
    "            if word.startswith(start):\n",
    "                return True\n",
    "    return False\n",
    "\n",
    "songs['has_profanity'] = songs['lyrics_words'].apply(has_profanity)"
   ]
  },
